{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: R11 item 6 (finding 3.8) and the BR-4 completion, one head. Head b42a624594df7b49a8667e70742d125b4af77ca7, tree 8a72ae9a, branch request/security-r11-20261027. Main 1b45fb0e is the merge base. The delta is 44 paths, 772 insertions and 45 deletions. Review request 48991996, checker promise d16ca094.\n- R11: request 183d7066, promise ee18ccc1, primary 94d1b9a2.\n- BR-4: request 15b0f8ab, promise f76f93d3, primary e114eb81.\n- Planner ruling 9c488459. All 49 artifacts at this head are cited.\n- gs inspect shows each primary resting on exactly its own promise and its own request.\n\nRead order: both notes in full; 183d7066 item 6 and finding 3.8 of 6dd06d03; 15b0f8ab; the production delta (applications/act-admission.ts in full, plus the core.ts, object.ts, ports.ts and worker.ts wiring, and the refusal reason in contract, bytes, mcp and metrics); the witness tests; the three control outputs; the final gate record; the manifest and the sealed directory. I did not run any suite again.\n\nR11 (finding 3.8: \"APPLICATION_TRUST revoked after an install: installed definitions keep judging acts\"):\n1. Admission. Scope.submit checks admission before any new dependency read, for intents whose key is not already accepted. It checks the store again after the admission read. A known key keeps its receipt, or its mismatch answer, with no admission read; turn.test.ts proves this with admission unavailable. The core rechecks at write, after the asynchronous reads (core.ts:650). A refused genesis bypasses admission and keeps scope-refused. Deliveries, timed rules, outcomes, replay and capability preparations do not pass through this path.\n2. Provenance. ApplicationActAdmission walks immutable native births, at most 18 ancestors, 37 bodies, 36 RPCs and 16 MiB. For each edge it checks:\n   - the creator's birth and the exact creator-source entry;\n   - the single send to this seed, and the use content;\n   - at the native Directory, the application-create delivery with the cohort's exact Directory pin;\n   - the Rules and Membership siblings sent by that Directory;\n   - the definition, the release, the semantic and presentation digests, the lane ordinal and the cause digest.\n   Platform-pinned scopes and genuine parentless founded births are unpackaged. Every other gap, including a missing births or proofs port, is \"unavailable\". Only the verified provenance is cached, keyed by canonical genesis identity. Trust is read on every use.\n3. Trust decision. A release in the current APPLICATION_TRUST is allowed. Absent, malformed or non-string trust gives application-revoked. A changed identity gives unavailable (dependency-unavailable).\n4. Witnesses.\n   - Native (application-owned-scopes): two installations with byte-identical definitions. After one release is withdrawn, its root and child refuse fresh acts with application-revoked, with no entry written, both warm and after a cold restart. The accepted act still returns its receipt, a changed intent under the same key gets mismatch, and settle still works. The other installation still accepts.\n   - Real Core (turn.test): a withdrawal during the authority read refuses at commit.\n5. Controls (raw output read). Disabling the current-trust guard makes the Native witness accept (\"fresh acts under the withdrawn exact release must refuse\"). Disabling the commit recheck makes the turn witness accept. Both mutants compile. The earlier commit-recheck control did not compile; it is recorded as inconclusive.\n6. The partition witness keeps its original 17 and 29 proof reads. It now also checks, separately, the admission reads that come first: 1 for the root and 7 for the depth-four receiver.\n7. Request 183d7066: R9 landed in Main 56de7567 (receipt f5ef1452) and R10 in e83a1ee5 (receipt 598cd48b). Both are ancestors of 1b45fb0e, so this head delivers the last item, 6. The head states the choice (a named refusal, with no revocation act).\n\nBR-4 (15b0f8ab), all five acceptance outcomes:\n- Lending reason and fetch category, and the archive-git-v2-layout failure detail: these came in with Main 1b45fb0e.\n- The command limit of at least three times its median: from the capture head, ruling eb0cc06e.\n- The 4,800-input floor row is gone. The 10-input case (8 alarms, null stopped and floor, exact confirmation) and the 29,000-entry backlog witnesses remain, and the 4,800-entry cadence witness is unchanged.\n- A stuck fixture owner: when close rejects while the owner still holds the clock, the owner is marked failed. Later fixture calls skip with the fixed reason \"Native archive fixture skipped: prior close failed; ownership retained\", before any resource or hook exists. The original failure keeps the run nonzero, and a setup error and a close error are both kept.\n- The negative probe exits 1 with one failed case and three named skips, including after a real late settlement. In the compiled control without the skip branch, all three successors fail with overlap errors and the verifier rejects.\n\nValidation:\n- Both earlier gates stay recorded as failures: cef0b72c (generated bundles) and edb48d85 (two Native failures and one unresolved teardown RPC error, cause not established).\n- The fresh ordinary gate at 577928b6 (tree 81c0462f) passed: exit 0, 1,177.366 s wall, 2,068.514 s child CPU (one run). Node 57, Counting 55, plain 2,848 passed and 1 skipped, Native 795 passed and 2 skipped. No contradictory records and no unhandled errors.\n- After the gate only the two notes and the manifest change, so the documents-only rule applies.\n- The manifest (sha256 09046d49) verifies against the sealed directory: 223 files, 0 bad, nothing writable, SHA256SUMS all OK. check-notes 1b45fb0e..b42a6245 reports 0 warnings, and git diff --check is clean.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Admission is a deployment port. DeployedScope wires it from env.APPLICATION_TRUST, and raw engine wiring is unchanged. It writes no entry, changes no recorded judgment or replay, and adds no setting or migration. Cost: the first fresh act on a cold object in a package lineage pays the provenance walk, up to 36 native RPCs (7 in the depth-four witness). After that it reuses the cached provenance until restart.\n\nSecurity: the finding is closed for installations. No blocking finding. Two points for the planner:\n1. Rollout. Deploying this head acts at once as a withdrawal for every installed room whose release is not in that Worker's APPLICATION_TRUST, including a Worker where the setting is absent. Before each deploy, list the releases installed in live rooms and confirm that each one you intend to keep is in that Worker's list.\n2. Scope of the rule. The refusal follows the installed release recorded at creation, not the definition bytes. A scope created from the same definition digest by another native path (for example a lane whose definition the rules scope activated) is unpackaged and not refused. That matches finding 3.8 (\"installed definitions\"), and the note states it (\"two releases can share every definition digest without sharing this decision\").\n\nSimplification: acceptable. One bounded module with a single cache slot and one flight. The cohort table repeats the cohort list that other readers hold; BR-13's version tables could own it later.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head b42a6245. The builder lands. The landing closes R11 request 183d7066 (its last item) and BR-4 request 15b0f8ab (all five outcomes). Parent 0f0eeab7 and R14 child 00abd5aa stay open. No builder deployment; the planner deploys after the rollout check above.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:94d1b9a2404cc557b05127a72f03cfdf23e777f8","binding":"assigned","head":"b42a624594df7b49a8667e70742d125b4af77ca7","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d16ca09453a7d69bf75857531eb7c26585171cb6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ee18ccc18e5689c2592202a2226ff0c516255ea9\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f76f93d31bc4bc0f97eb63bbf8ca28375daceb03\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d16ca09453a7d69bf75857531eb7c26585171cb6","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}